`Effect.Error` is the base class to extend when creating a tagged error type in Effect-TS. This allows leveraging the error handling mechanisms provided by the Effect library, including tagged error patterns.

Example usage:
```typescript
import { Effect } from "effect-ts";

class MyError extends Effect.Error {
  static readonly TAG = "MyError";
  constructor(public readonly message: string) {
    super(message);
    this.name = MyError.TAG;
  }
}
```

**Note**: Ensure the error type adheres to Effect's requirements (e.g., `name` property set to the tag) to work with its runtime and tagged error features.

